		"about": "The verbs lessons are made for, most used first, each with the English the learner reads: base, she-form, before, and the ing form. Part 1 of every job is the grid's own lesson, so the first verb here is Part 2. `no-going` marks the verbs that do not take sedang on their own (coming, sitting, getting up); `no-command` the commands that are right and nobody says (Fly! Cry!). Left out on purpose: pergi, which the grid's own lessons teach; ada and adalah, which need lessons of their own; mau, bisa and harus, which are the want-can-must job; membaca, whose English is the same now and before; and menyetir, which the dump does not have as a verb.",
